    ("await-always-hands-off", "Every await gives another task an execution turn", "A CPython 3.14.7 completed built-in Future and a Rust 1.90 Ready child can let the awaiting body continue without an intervening executor turn. Normally prepared ECMAScript Await suspends and resumes through reactions, but that does not promise a browser timer runs first.", "py-ready-await"),
    ("async-future-construction-runs-body", "Calling a Rust async function immediately runs its async body", "The call constructs its generated future; polling drives that body's steps. Arguments can still be evaluated at the call site, and a different API can start background work before returning a future handle.", "rust-future-create"),
    ("wake-means-ready", "A wake proves the operation is ready and guarantees one distinct poll", "A wake requests another poll of the unfinished task. Notifications can coalesce, a later poll can still return Pending, and executor-specific dispatch behavior is not a universal deferred-call or next-task ordering rule.", "wake-call"),
