    ("task-construction-never-runs-code", "Python create_task can never run body code before returning", "CPython 3.14.7 non-eager scheduling and eager start have different initial traces. An applicable eager setting can execute the coroutine prefix during task construction until an actual suspension or completion.", "py-eager-start"),
    ("accepted-cancel-guarantees-parent-exception", "A successful Python Task.cancel call guarantees cancellation is injected into that parent", "Cancellation may be delegated to the child Task being awaited. In CPython 3.14.7 that child can catch cancellation and return normally, allowing the parent to resume without receiving CancelledError even while its cancelling count remains positive.", "py-cancel-request"),
