    ("python-cancellation-delivery-boundary", "Accepted cancellation and executed cleanup are distinct", "In CPython 3.14.7 a child can absorb cancellation delegated by its awaiting parent. A task cancelled before body entry need not enter its try/finally at all. Cleanup claims therefore require an already-active scope and propagation through it; suppression can yield a normal result without clearing the request count.", "py-cancel-request"),
    ("structured-membership-boundary", "A group owns registered members rather than every task in sight", "TaskGroup waits for its registered members and distinguishes ordinary failure, child cancellation, and KeyboardInterrupt/SystemExit. Default gather has a different sibling-cancellation policy. Shield protects only the named propagation path and needs a retained inner task; it does not make the outer caller immune to cancellation or adopt all background work.", "py-taskgroup"),
    ("timeout-cooperation-boundary", "Timeout observation depends on loop and cancellation progress", "A timeout callback cannot preempt synchronous loop-thread code. wait_for can outlast its deadline while awaiting cancellation cleanup or return a child value after cancellation suppression. timeout-context conversion concerns its own propagated cancellation at exit, with outside catching and independent cancellation races kept separate.", "timeout-error"),
    ("queue-accounting-boundary", "Join observes accounting rather than external success", "CPython 3.14.7 task_done decrements a counter; the API does not verify that the caller previously dequeued or successfully processed an item. Immediate shutdown uses max(U-Q,0) for unfinished count U and drained queued count Q. With disciplined post-dequeue acknowledgments, already-dequeued unfinished work remains counted; no join result proves storage durability or application success.", "join-return"),
